</figure>
<figure id="S5.F19" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04076v1/Figs/Soft-Robot.png" id="S5.F19.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:346/231;" width="346" height="231" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 19: </span>Reference Tracking by Soft Robotic Arm. Experimental results video: <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yTN6vKkndDg</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.F20" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04076v1/Figs/Soft-Output.png" id="S5.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:346/259;" width="346" height="259" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 20: </span>Reference tracking for Soft Robotic Arm.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Soft Robotic Arm Motion Control:</span>
Another experimental study was carried out on a pneumatically actuated soft robotic arm to evaluate the performance of DeePC and reduced-order DeePC <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>, as illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S5.F19" title="Fig. 19 ‣ V Real-Time Implementation ‣ From Shadow to Light: Toward Safe and Efficient Policy Learning Across MPC, DeePC, RL, and LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>. The I/O data, defined as the chamber pressure and the end-effector coordinates in task space, were collected under randomized excitation and organized into Hankel matrix. The control objective involved tracking sinusoidal trajectories in both the <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> directions, where an interpolation function <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> was employed to capture the coupled underactuated dynamics and ensure feasible reference trajectories. The soft robot was equipped with a Qualisys motion capture system, providing accurate real-time measurements of the end-effector position for closed-loop tracking.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE III: </span>Comparison of Performance and Computational Time for DeePC and Reduced-Order DeePC</figcaption>
